From 9a9d92dc33856d9a6c403a6db8c22c97077ce839 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 07:09:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CssStyleEngine: make media-query evaluation follow the MQ4
 grammar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three defects in the media-query evaluator, all with the same shape: a query
the engine could not evaluate collapsed to `false`, and a leading `not` then
turned it into a match.

1. An empty <media-query-list> evaluated to false. It is equivalent to `all`
   and must match, so `@media { … }` — whitespace after the at-keyword is
   optional — and `<style media="">` now apply unconditionally.
   (WPT css/css-conditional/at-media-whitespace-optional-001)

2. `layer` was treated as an unknown media type, so `@media not layer` matched
   and painted the test's red failure background. css-cascade-5 reserves the
   ident for `@import … layer`, so it is excluded from <media-type> alongside
   the boolean keywords: both `@media layer` and `@media not layer` are
   malformed and become `not all`.
   (WPT css/mediaqueries/mq-invalid-media-type-layer-002)

3. An unrecognised feature, an unparsable feature value, a range feature in
   boolean context and a media type after `and` all returned false, so their
   negations matched everything. MQ4 distinguishes "does not match" from "does
   not parse": a malformed query is replaced by `not all`, and an unknown
   feature is <general-enclosed> whose value is *unknown*. Both stay false
   through `not`, which a bool cannot express — evaluation is now tri-state
   (NoMatch / Match / Invalid).

Keeping known-but-non-matching features negatable meant filling in the feature
table the tri-state would otherwise have marked invalid: the <length>, <ratio>,
<integer> and <resolution> range features in their plain/min-/max- forms, and
the discrete features (orientation, pointer, hover, forced-colors, scripting,
prefers-*, …) with their keyword sets, so an out-of-range keyword is malformed
while a valid non-matching one still negates.
